.TH IFCONFIG 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
ifconfig \- show the network interfaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ifconfig
.RI [ interface ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ifconfig
shows the computer's network interfaces, its network cards: each one's
name, flags and MTU, then its address
.RB ( ether ),
the card's id, which other computers send to (as a network card's MAC
address). Wired cards are named
.BR eth0 ,
.BR eth1 ,
\&... and WLAN cards
.BR wlan0 ,
.BR wlan1 ,
\&... in bus order. With an
.IR interface ,
only that one.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when there's no such interface.
.SH NOTES
Linux's
.B ifconfig
also configures interfaces and shows their IP addresses and counters;
mcos has no IP, and nothing of an interface to configure but its
Wake\-on\-LAN
.RB ( ethtool ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nc (1),
.BR ethtool (1),
.BR lsdev (1)
